The attached image illustrates the dendrimer-like alpha-D-glucan nanoparticle, termed Nano-11, which is a key component of the vaccine adjuvant studied in the PDF. The schematic depicts a spherical particle with a dense, highly branched internal structure, characteristic of a dendrimer. This structure is formed from phytoglycogen due to a debranching enzyme deficiency, replacing starch granules. Its dendrimer-like nature, with high molecular density, contributes to its efficient antigen adsorption and delivery to dendritic cells, enhancing the immune response as described in the research.